    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, both tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date rule: when no `registrationDate` is supplied on owner creation it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form.\n\n**Design for low structural impact** \u2014 the default logic lives in one trivial setter on the `Owner` entity, mirroring the existing null-guarding `setEmail` pattern, so MapStruct maps the field by name and no controller/mapper/service method had to change. Changed functions are just two new trivial accessors (CC 1) rather than editing any complex, high-WMC method.\n\nFiles touched (4):\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated DTOs gain the field (writable on input, returned on output). No functions.\n- **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` column plus getter and a setter that defaults `null \u2192 LocalDate.now()`. This is the sole behavior change and it's a 2-line self-contained unit.\n- **`src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared here, just like `email`).\n- **`src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing seed value to the positional owner inserts to match the new column (again mirroring how `email` was handled).\n\nJackson serializes `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the test's `LocalDate.now().toString()` expectation and the kept-supplied `\"2020-06-15\"` case.",
